# CODEOWNERS — an ownership MAP, not an enforced review gate
#
# This file exists for REVIEW-ROUTING and ACCOUNTABILITY: it records who is
# responsible for the trust-critical and release-critical surfaces of this
# repository, so a change to any of them is automatically routed to that owner
# for review and there is a named owner of record for each path.
#
# It is deliberately a MAP and nothing more. Mandatory two-person review is
# intentionally NOT (yet) enforced via GitHub branch protection — this is a
# small team, and a required-reviewer rule with a single effective maintainer
# blocks its own releases with no second reviewer to unblock them. That is a
# documented, revisitable decision (H6d), not an oversight. When the team grows
# a second trusted reviewer, the intended follow-up is to turn on branch
# protection with CODEOWNERS review REQUIRED on these same paths.
#
# Because review is not force-blocked, the release runbook documents the
# emergency / break-glass release path a solo maintainer uses (the local
# scripted-release path and the rollback procedure) — see docs/releasing.md.
#
# Syntax: gitignore-style patterns, most-specific-last wins. A leading "/"
# anchors to the repo root; a trailing "/" matches a directory tree.

# ── Trust core: signing, verification, revocation, trust roots ───────────────
/pkg/skillctl/signing/     @kamir
/pkg/skillctl/verify/      @kamir
/pkg/skillctl/trustcore/   @kamir
/pkg/skillbundle/          @kamir

# ── Registry, scanner, propose (admission + version/trust decisions) ─────────
/pkg/skillctl/registry/    @kamir
/pkg/skillctl/scanner/     @kamir
/pkg/skillctl/propose/     @kamir

# ── The trust CLI and the safe HTTP surface ──────────────────────────────────
/cmd/skillctl/             @kamir
/pkg/httpsafe/             @kamir

# ── CI, release build + signing config, supply-chain bootstrap ───────────────
/.github/workflows/        @kamir
/.goreleaser.yml           @kamir
/scripts/release*.sh       @kamir
/scripts/skillctl-smoke.sh @kamir
/tools/skillctl-install.sh   @kamir
/tools/skillctl-install.ps1  @kamir

# ── Trust-root / signing configuration (pinned release public key) ───────────
/INFRA/                    @kamir

# ── Governance & security documents ──────────────────────────────────────────
/THREAT_MODEL.md           @kamir
/SECURITY.md               @kamir
/COMPATIBILITY.md          @kamir
/docs/releasing.md         @kamir
/.github/CODEOWNERS        @kamir
